  "name": "GAD-65 (GLUTAMIC ACID DECARBOXYLASE -65) - IgG",
  "code": "2748",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"90\" data-end=\"114\">GAD-65 antibody test</strong> detects <strong data-start=\"123\" data-end=\"145\">IgG autoantibodies</strong> against the <strong data-start=\"158\" data-end=\"215\">65-kDa isoform of glutamic acid decarboxylase (GAD65)</strong>, an enzyme present in pancreatic beta cells and certain neurons. This test is primarily used to evaluate for <strong data-start=\"325\" data-end=\"348\">autoimmune diabetes</strong> and other autoimmune neurological disorders.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (Detected)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests the presence of <strong>autoimmune activity</strong>, most commonly against pancreatic beta cells. Seen in:</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul data-start=\"1071\" data-end=\"1467\">\n<li data-start=\"1071\" data-end=\"1135\">\n<p data-start=\"1073\" data-end=\"1135\">Type 1 Diabetes (especially early or pre-symptomatic stages)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1136\" data-end=\"1200\">\n<p data-start=\"1138\" data-end=\"1200\">LADA (in adults initially misdiagnosed with type 2 diabetes)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1201\" data-end=\"1467\">\n<p data-start=\"1203\" data-end=\"1467\">Certain neurologic autoimmune diseases (if clinical features are present) |<br>| <strong data-start=\"1281\" data-end=\"1308\">Negative (Not Detected)</strong> | No detectable GAD-65 antibodies. Does <strong data-start=\"1349\" data-end=\"1376\">not completely rule out</strong> autoimmune diabetes or neurological conditions, as other autoantibodies may be involved.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
